request.description:
Can the BROWSER upload to this bucket? Separate from "Test connection" because the two fail independently: credentials can be perfect while every browser upload 403s in preflight for want of a bucket CORS rule.

**Auth:** bearer · requires `settings.integrations.storage.manage`.

**Returns:** `{ state, requiredOrigins, allowedOrigins, canApply, message, detail, policy }` where `state` is one of:
- `ok` — every required origin may PUT;
- `missing` — the bucket has no CORS configuration at all;
- `origin-not-allowed` — rules exist but not for our origin (`allowedOrigins` says which);
- `cannot-check` — the credentials may not read bucket config (an object-scoped R2 token); `canApply:false`, and `detail` carries the vendor's own words;
- `unconfigured` — no storage provider configured yet.

`policy` is the exact JSON to paste into the Cloudflare dashboard when we can't apply it.

